  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-826855",
   "speaker": "Rachel Siewert",
   "party": "Greens",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-12-12",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "Opposing most provisions in the Social Services and Other Legislation Amendment Bill 2013, the Greens criticised the government for rushing through 13 separate measures including university funding cuts, a freeze on the childcare rebate indexation, delaying the Charities Act 2013, extending income management in Cape York, and removing employer roles in paid parental leave; Labor supported some measures such as extending indexation pauses on higher family payment thresholds and closing the Pension Bonus Scheme but opposed the interest charge on student welfare debts, the childcare rebate freeze, and the last-minute postponement of the Charities Act definition."
  }
